    {
      "_id": "QcFB2Q8ZU08qZ14T",
      "_key": "!journal.pages!uhtM1iF2WrHHlcd8.QcFB2Q8ZU08qZ14T",
      "name": "Storyteller Notes",
      "type": "text",
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<p>The fresh flowers are the core of @UUID[JournalEntry.AnZpyM4onyACPwiC.JournalEntryPage.cGEW4b4hCJlaDeSK]{GAN-12 · The Visited Grave}. Who leaves them is left open for the chronicle (Marcos from @UUID[JournalEntry.AnZpyM4onyACPwiC.JournalEntryPage.pCLncsxglYsxJtbu]{GAN-01 · The Boy Who Survived}, someone from Salt&#39;s, or someone who signs “M.V.”).</p>\n<p>It appears in the Epilogue of @UUID[JournalEntry.ll97TEj4MRjtM595]{Chapter 7 · The Ward File} as one of the three possible codas.</p>\n<p>Use as a lost Touchstone: a visit lets David make a Remorse test with one extra die, but it also makes him ask himself a question he doesn&#39;t want to ask.</p>\n"
      },
